#
#   IPSum › Threat Intelligence Feeds
#   
#   A threat intelligence feed based on 30+ different publicly available
#   lists of suspicious and/or malicious IP addresses. All lists are
#   automatically retrieved and parsed on a daily (every 24 hours) basis
#   and the final result is pushed to this repository.
#   
#   IPSum is a collection of 8 different blocklists which are broken into
#   levels. The level number indicates how many blocklists a specific IP
#   was detected in. The higher the number, the more hits, and the higher
#   likelihood of it not being a false-positive.
#       
#       level1.txt          Lowest confidence. IPs seen in 1 blacklist.
#                               Highest false-positive rate.
#       level2.txt          Low confidence. IPs seen in 2 blacklists.
#       level3.txt          Moderate-low confidence. IPs seen in 3 blacklists.
#       level4.txt          Moderate confidence. IPs seen in 4 blacklists.
#       level5.txt          Moderate confidence. IPs seen in 5 blacklists.
#       level6.txt          High confidence. IPs seen in 6 blacklists.
#       level7.txt          Very high confidenc. IPs seen in 7 blacklists.
#       level8.txt          Highest confidence. IPs seen in 8 blacklists.
#                               Lowest false-positive rate.
#   
#   Github Repository:
#       https://github.com/stamparm/ipsum
#   
#   This third-party blocklist is not maintained by ConfigServer; IPs are
#   sourced externally and not curated by us. We do however, validate the
#   blocklist to ensure that it only contains properly validated IP addresses,
#   and does not include any non-relevant or malicious data beyond the scope
#   of the source.
#   
#   Use at the administrator's discretion based on risk tolerance and
#   environment requirements.
# #

